OK, so I recently posted about my _intensely_ bad luck with Rogues.

Well, my current Rogue must have gotten all the luck the previous ones
missed out on.  Check this out:

On level 2, a big general store with a few wands.  "OK, time to
engrave-ID them, hope for a wand of fire/cold/lightning, and zap the
shopkeeper til he stops moving".

Got a wand of cold.  Nice.  Tried the next wand.  "For what do you
wish?"

...

2 blessed scrolls of charging.
+2 GDSM.
a blessed wand of death.
a blessed bag of holding (for all me booty, arr!)
the blessed rustproof Stormbringer (I was feeling bloodthirsty)

Mind you, I had already found a magic marker as well.  Needless to
say, that shopkeeper is now hanging out in Limbo.

Then, just to make it really absurd, I found three or four more shops
_in the main dungeon_ before I even hit the Oracle.  One was an huge
scroll shop; one was an huge potion shop.

To top it off, Sokoban gave me the amulet.

Swift the Rogue is currently level 11, bought protection down to
natural AC of 2, and is running around #two-weaponing +6 Stormy and a
+7 silver saber, with roughly 30 blank scrolls and 30 holy waters.

Oh, and did I mention he found a ring of poly control as well?

The only annoying thing so far is that my pet Djinni (from a blessed
smoky potion) became un-tame when I left him alone on a level for
literally only about 10 moves.  Is there any way to increase tameness
besides food (since Djinn don't eat)?  I had thought that casting
